From c1e39662698f573f8137cac45dcd382f1da6c750 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "VTSTech (Nigel Todman)" <veritas@vts-tech.org>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:01:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Add shader base resolution (-vkbase /
 shader_base_resolution)

DevilutionX-style dual-resolution model for the Vulkan presenter: the
window/swapchain keeps Chocolate Doom's regular sizing while the canvas
handed to the slang chain can be independently enlarged 2x/3x/4x.

- feed is duplicated k-fold (exact k x k nearest blocks, no new detail)
  after the palette LUT expansion and before the preset chain runs
- chain input image + staging sized feed x k (cap 4: 1280x960); the
  chain re-derives every pass FBO from the per-frame input size, so
  upscaler presets (HQx, ScaleFX) get real input-to-output headroom
- one LUT pass per source row + memcpy for the k-1 duplicates
- -vkbase <n> accepts the multiplier (2/3/4) or a pixel width
  (640/960/1280); config key shader_base_resolution (0 = native)
- startup log prints the effective choice; F11 aspect toggle composes
  (base follows the feed); stats overlay row 4 shows the live canvas
  (e.g. "640x480 4:3 (2x)")

Validated on lavapipe: six-run matrix (1x/2x/width-form/headroom/4x+
validation layers/config-seeded 3x), overlay decoded from every
capture, content equivalence vs the 1x baseline (mean diff <= 9.9/255;
scan-corrected ratio median exactly 1.000 at 3x), zero validation
messages at 4x, timedemo throughput ~294/211/157/117 fps at 1x/2x/3x/4x.
